# shell: desktop
# CW-020: a folder's background picture is shown in an icon mode and taken
# away in list view, because a picture behind a table of text is unreadable.
key 1 ctrl
wait 8
note the picture is tiled over the window, so a point well away from any
note icon is the picture's own colour -- BMP keeps its bytes blue first, so
note the fixture's 32,64,192 is c04020 on screen -- rather than the ground
expect-pixel 300 220 c04020
note switching to list view takes it away
key 3 ctrl
wait 8
expect-pixel 300 220 ffffff
note and leaving list view brings it back
key 1 ctrl
wait 8
expect-pixel 300 220 c04020
note PVL-071: a label over the picture is haloed, so it stays readable
note wherever the picture happens to be the colour of the text -- white
note around the letters, and the letters themselves still in the ink
expect-pixel 209 146 ffffff
expect-pixel 210 147 000000
quit
